<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="theme-color" content="#0b1119"><title>Getting started · FloodWatch</title><link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700&family=Space+Mono&display=swap" rel="stylesheet"><link rel="stylesheet" href="assets/dashboard.css"><style>.setup-wrap{width:min(740px,100%);margin:0 auto;padding:54px 24px 70px}.setup-brand{margin-bottom:30px}.setup-card{margin:13px 0;padding:20px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:6px;background:var(--surface)}.setup-card h2{margin:0 0 9px;font-size:14px;font-weight:600}.setup-card p,.setup-card li{color:#97a5b0;font-size:11px;line-height:1.8}.setup-card ol{padding-left:20px}.setup-card li+li{margin-top:6px}.setup-card pre{overflow-x:auto;margin:11px 0 0;padding:13px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:5px;background:#0b1119;color:#94ddbc;font:10px/1.8 'Space Mono',monospace;white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.setup-back{display:inline-flex;margin-bottom:12px;color:#77d8b6;font-size:11px;text-decoration:none}.setup-note{padding:10px 13px;border:1px solid #554528;border-radius:5px;background:#241f16;color:#ddc58c;font-size:10px}</style></head>
<body><main class="setup-wrap"><a class="brand setup-brand" href="<?= htmlspecialchars($base ?: '/', ENT_QUOTES, 'UTF-8') ?>/"><span class="brand-mark"><svg viewBox="0 0 28 28" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M14 3C11 8 6 13.4 6 18a8 8 0 0 0 16 0c0-4.6-5-10-8-15Z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8"/><path d="M10 19c.4 2 1.6 3 3.5 3" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></span><span>Flood<span class="brand-light">Watch</span><small>LOCAL MONITORING</small></span></a><a class="setup-back" href="<?= htmlspecialchars($base ?: '/', ENT_QUOTES, 'UTF-8') ?>/">← Back to monitoring</a><div class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-line"></span> QUICK START</div><h1>Connect your sensors<span class="heading-period">.</span></h1><p class="page-subtitle">A local MySQL database stores every reading, right on your network.</p>
<section class="setup-card"><h2>01 · Create the database</h2><p>In XAMPP, start <strong>Apache</strong> and <strong>MySQL</strong>. Open phpMyAdmin at <code>http://localhost/phpmyadmin/</code>, select the <strong>Import</strong> tab, and import <code>schema.sql</code>.</p><p>The default connection uses the XAMPP settings: database <code>flood_monitor</code>, user <code>root</code>, no password. If your MySQL credentials differ, edit <code>config.php</code> or set <code>FLOOD_DB_HOST</code>, <code>FLOOD_DB_NAME</code>, <code>FLOOD_DB_USER</code>, and <code>FLOOD_DB_PASSWORD</code> in the Apache environment.</p></section>
<section class="setup-card"><h2>02 · Send readings from your ESP32</h2><p>Have the ESP32 issue an HTTP POST to <code><?= htmlspecialchars($ingestUrl, ENT_QUOTES, 'UTF-8') ?></code> for every sensor sample. Replace <code>192.168.1.x</code> with your computer's LAN IP address. Both devices need to be on the same local network.</p><pre>POST <?= htmlspecialchars($ingestUrl, ENT_QUOTES, 'UTF-8') ?>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "water_level_cm": 18.2,
  "distance_cm": 6.8,
  "temperature_c": 29.4,
  "humidity_pct": 82,
  "rain_detected": true,
  "rain_probability_pct": 65,
  "alert_level": "warning"
}</pre><p>Required: <code>water_level_cm</code>. Rain probability, rain detection, and the temperature and humidity fields accept values from the ESP32. Supported alerts are <code>normal</code>, <code>watch</code>, <code>warning</code>, and <code>danger</code>. The dashboard calculates water-level rise rate and estimated time to danger from your recorded samples.</p><p>Set <code>INGEST_API_KEY</code> in <code>config.php</code> if you want to authenticate writes from your LAN.</p></section>
<section class="setup-card"><h2>03 · Open the dashboard</h2><p>Visit <code><?= htmlspecialchars($origin . '/', ENT_QUOTES, 'UTF-8') ?></code> on the server, or use your computer's LAN address when viewing the site on another device. The dashboard refreshes readings every 15 seconds and lets you export historical readings as CSV.</p><p>The included demonstration data is only a visual preview. Live readings, connectivity indicators, and CSV export activate when MySQL is set up and receives sensor measurements.</p></section><p class="setup-note">The rain probability is recorded from the ESP32; a DHT11 measures temperature and humidity, not rain. Connect a rain sensor or provide a forecast value to populate rain readings.</p></main></body></html>
